Windows overrides of the speech synthesis engine

The Windows build of the speaking library (CMakeLists.txt, one directory up)
compiles these two files in place of the engine's own files of the same name
(MIMI_OVERRIDE, ACOUSTIC_OVERRIDE). Both are modified copies of files of
audio.cpp, Copyright 2026 ShugoAI LLC, at revision
3174e6b26f11a0e39b4f150961dce98f43ba860d, under the Apache License, Version
2.0, which is this repository's licence too (LICENSE, at its root). Each file
in this directory is listed here with where it comes from and what was changed.
The engine source the build is given (ENGINE_SOURCE) is not that revision's as
it stands either: five more files of it are replaced, and ../../engine_overrides
holds them with their own notice.

acoustic_model.cpp
  Upstream: src/models/pocket_tts/acoustic_model.cpp
  Upstream sha256: 5cd1e0e79ecbd7a1bea21704946f0237c72fc3c2f021c1c4228024c96c4d46f6
  As built sha256: 81a40bcb089e48dac1dc351f3ca189da282e6907270e390053a9af08a84481eb
  Changed: one line. In AcousticModel::next_stream_step, a stream that
  reaches its frame limit before a natural end is an error ("PocketTTS
  reached its frame limit before natural EOS and tail completion") where
  upstream returns no step. Nothing else differs.
  This file does NOT carry the change capacity-history.patch makes to the
  same upstream file (the cached step runtime reused only at exactly the
  prompt capacity asked for): the reuse condition here is upstream's.

mimi_decoder.cpp
  Upstream: src/models/pocket_tts/mimi_decoder.cpp
  Upstream sha256: d64e4f1b6102d5d3a35f32eed6805ea6a232b055cfca253108e0520723fc5fc4
  As built sha256: 29d6fd43febf041ea8e6c202e29d5920680e05b9125c658af28c5960a3347fc5
  Changed: in three places. In two, where the decoder builds a streaming
  transformer block, four lines became three: the block is configured through
  graph_common::pocket_transformer_config (../../engine_overrides/NOTICE), with
  the values upstream writes there. In the third, seventeen lines are added:
  after the decoder's transformer graph is built, the key and value tensors,
  the prefix keys and values and the attention mask are marked as outputs of
  the graph, so that the graph allocator does not reuse their storage at their
  last use inside the graph: the owner copies them into the next step's state
  after the graph has run. Nothing else differs.
  The engine directory of the Windows build holds this file without the
  seventeen lines (sha256
  23070cfd247aedea5e1c84e157d0918266402ae3a320788f01e0092e85c7329a); the
  engine's own library is compiled from that directory, and the speaking
  library compiles the file here.

"As built" is the file the Windows runtimes' library was built from, which
is the file here without its four-line head comment; a test holds the two
to that. "Upstream" is the file of the upstream repository at the revision
above. Before this notice these two files were in no repository: they were
taken from the directory that library was built in.

Three more files of audio.cpp are adapted for the same library, for reading
models by handle inside a contained Windows process: src/framework/assets/
resource_bundle.cpp, src/framework/io/filesystem.cpp and src/framework/io/
safetensors.cpp, with a header paths.h written for this project. They are
not kept as files: scripts/stage_native_path_shim.py derives them from the
three unmodified upstream files (tests/fixtures/native_path_upstream, with
their licence), and its regression reverses the derivation byte for byte.
